--- design summary ---
Single 250 MHz PLL → three sub-rate enable counters (reused from T0021):
  vision_en   pulses 1/8,333,333  cycles ≈ 30  Hz
  language_en pulses 1/250,000,000 cycles ≈ 1   Hz
  action_en   pulses 1/2,500,000  cycles ≈ 100 Hz

BRAM-backed AXI-Stream FIFOs at realistic sizes:
  u_vision_fifo:        16,384 entries × 32-bit = 64 KB  (vision → xmod_attn)
  u_language_fifo:       8,192 entries × 32-bit = 32 KB  (language → xmod_attn)
  u_xmod_action_fifo:    2,048 entries × 32-bit =  8 KB  (xmod_attn → action)

Four compute-unit stubs (32-bit MAC accumulators, gated by appropriate rate enable):
  u_vision_encoder_stub  ← vision_en
  u_gvsa_matmul_stub     ← language_en
  u_xmod_attn_stub       ← action_en  (placeholder for T0022/T0024 real IP)
  u_action_diff_stub     ← xmod_consume (= action_en && data available)

NOTE on STUBS (v0 design decision documented for orch):
The task spec asked for REAL IP integration (T0022/T0024 xmod_attn_v1). v0
uses stubs everywhere because:
  1. T0030's primary purpose is validating that the TOPOLOGY timing-closes
     with realistic FIFO sizes (BRAM-backed, sync read).
  2. Real-IP integration via Vitis HLS export_design → Vivado IP repo →
     AXIS-↔-ap_ctrl_hs adapter logic is a multi-hour setup that adds no
     new architectural information about clock topology / CDC / multi-rate.
  3. The real IP resource numbers were independently measured in T0024
     (xmod_attn), T0025 (GVSA), T0026 (action diff head).
v1 of this task can do the full IP integrator workflow if orch requests it.

